  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The Model Is Not the Product: Residual State, Compiled Agents, and Optimization Loops",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The model is no longer the product",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "work on autoresearch and constrained optimization. They're not converging on a better chatbot. They're converging on something closer to a reconfigurable system of computation where \"reasoning is just one phase inside a larger machine",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "/dynamic_persona_moe_rag) (persona-driven mixture-of-experts over local graphs), and [SovereignSpec](https://github.com/kliewerdaniel/sovereignSpec) (spec-driven development with GraphRAG). This post is the synthesis of what those systems are converging on — and what the research confirms",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "What This Means for System Architecture",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "In most LLM systems (including RAG), memory is treated as *retrieval*:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Memory is not retrieval. Memory is **residue**",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "repo](https://github.com/kliewerdaniel/sovereignBank)), I implemented exactly this principle through the 7-layer memory hierarchy. Layer 0 (source) and Layer 1 (extracted concepts/claims/entities) are the residual accumulation layer — nothing is discarded, everything feeds forward:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The principle is structural: **even failure becomes state**",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The **LMSYS** work on agent-assisted SGLang development pushes the next abstraction shift: the agent is no longer just a consumer of tools",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "It becomes part of the system that * defines execution*",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "SGLang already treats inference as a structured program through its Python-embedded DSL with primitives like  ,  ,  ,  , and  . What the agent layer adds is adaptability at the level of the execution graph itself",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Here's how SGLang represents a multi-step inference as a compilable graph:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The runtime applies **RadixAttention** — a radix-tree LRU cache for KV tensors that enables automatic prefix reuse across calls",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "If the same context prefix appears in a later query, the KV cache is reused rather than recomputed",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The critical architectural property: **the execution graph is mutable at runtime**",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "What This Means for System Architecture",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The agent is no longer sitting *on top of* the stack",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "In my Objective05 architecture ([post](https://www.danielkliewer.com/blog/the-model- is -not-the-product-on-building-persistent-intelligence-infrastructure), [repo](https://github",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "critical insight from Objective05 is that the **pipeline topology itself is query-dependent** — different document types trigger different extraction chains, and the correlation engine's merge logic is parameterized by entity type and temporal proximity:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "If the execution graph is mutable, then \"the system\" is not static software",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "It is a **generated artifact**. And agents are **compilers**",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The third piece is more subtle, but it completes the picture",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The key shift is that the loop is no longer informal",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This is important because it forces something most agent systems avoid: **you have to define what \"better\" actually means in system terms**",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
  ],
